WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.280
TV romances are a cherished part of&nbsp;
pop culture. Uncle Phil and Aunt Viv,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:12.400
Jim and Pam, Cory and Topanga—we love them all.&nbsp;
But some TV couples are downright unhealthy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.920
These are the most rotten&nbsp;
romances in television history.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:23.120
Buffy the Vampire Slayer’s Spike and Buffy&nbsp;
epitomize toxicity. Long before they hook up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.560
Spike develops a creepy infatuation with Buffy&nbsp;
after his longtime girlfriend and fellow vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:35.040
Drusilla dumps him. When Buffy brutally rejects&nbsp;
him, he gets Warren, evil nerd extraordinaire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.800
to create a creepy robot in her likeness. Making&nbsp;
a sexbot of someone definitely isn't a healthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.560
way to deal with your feelings, Spike. Following&nbsp;
her death and subsequent resurrection, she feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.720
lost and hooks up with Spike—a lot—to escape her&nbsp;
hollowness, but ends up hating herself even more.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.120
Sure, Spike cares for her in his own twisted way.&nbsp;
But, when she finally comes to her senses and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.320
breaks things off with him, he tries to assault&nbsp;
her. In an attempt to earn her love and respect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.040
the vamp goes through hell to get a soul. While&nbsp;
their time together during his soulless days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.520
is toxic and horrible, he eventually&nbsp;
becomes the man that Buffy deserves.

00:01:15.756 --> 00:01:18.400
Miss Piggy and Kermit's 2015&nbsp;
breakup was a long time coming.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.760
When they first graced the screen as a couple&nbsp;
in the '70s on The Muppet Show, their toxic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:29.200
back-and-forth was played for laughs — but boy,&nbsp;
does it get brutal. Miss Piggy continuously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:34.480
punches her beau, who's also her boss. Talk&nbsp;
about an uncomfortable workplace dynamic.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:42.080
When ABC revived the series in 2015, domestic&nbsp;
abuse didn't play so funny anymore. In what was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.880
both a brilliant marketing campaign and the&nbsp;
right plot choice, the duo aired their messy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.480
split as part of the new series. And who better to&nbsp;
provide what was essentially couple's counseling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.920
than Jimmy Kimmel? Although their romance remains&nbsp;
dead, Miss Piggy and Kermit have worked together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.720
professionally since their split, on projects&nbsp;
like The Muppets and 2020's Muppets Now.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.720
Demon Ruby shows up on&nbsp;
Supernatural in season three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.640
quickly convincing Sam that she's on&nbsp;
their side while Dean remains skeptical.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:17.040
With Ruby’s original meat suit rotting somewhere,&nbsp;
Sam makes her possess the comatose body of a woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:23.200
who just died. From there, they develop romantic&nbsp;
feelings, partaking in typical couple stuff like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.720
hooking up and telekinetically exorcising demons.&nbsp;
When your girlfriend is force-feeding you demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.880
blood to supercharge said telekinesis, that should&nbsp;
probably raise some red flags. Yet Sam refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.680
see what's right in front of him until the demon&nbsp;
successfully coerces him into releasing Lucifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.200
from Hell. Ruby's response to manipulating&nbsp;
her boyfriend for over a year? "I'm awesome!"

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:51.520
However, it isn't all bad. Actress Genevieve&nbsp;
Cortese and Jared Padalecki fell in love during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.640
the steamy throes of on-screen demon passion,&nbsp;
and have since married and had multiple children.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.400
It's not surprising that a show&nbsp;
filmed in the '50s would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.440
a romanticized toxic marriage as the centerpiece.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.880
At first glance, it seems like Ricky and Lucy&nbsp;
from I Love Lucy have the perfect marriage. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.600
you’re quickly confronted with the toxic roles&nbsp;
women and men were expected to play in the '50s.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.560
Ricky often scolds Lucy for wanting to&nbsp;
spend time with him, and at one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.720
she thinks he's trying to kill her.&nbsp;
His response is to "give her a Mickey."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.320
Imagine how messed up a relationship has to be for&nbsp;
you to think your spouse is trying to kill you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.400
Imagine how much worse it is when his&nbsp;
response to your suspicions is to drug you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.040
Small scenes like this add up throughout the&nbsp;
show's run, creating a much different picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.240
of the supposedly happy couple&nbsp;
for modern viewers to cringe at.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.000
While Gilmore Girls' Dean Forester starts&nbsp;
out as the super sweet boy next door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.360
things quickly take a turn after he and Rory&nbsp;
begin dating. Everything Dean starts out loving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.800
about Rory turns into an issue, including her&nbsp;
academic studies, her relationship with her mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.440
and her compassion. Plus, any time Rory&nbsp;
dares to interact with another guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.520
even in an educational setting,&nbsp;
Dean flies into a possessive rage.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.320
Dean tries to control every facet of&nbsp;
Rory's life and blows up at her when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.840
she doesn't return his "I love you"&nbsp;
during their three-month anniversary.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.638
“Rory, I love you...Rory?”

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:19.680
“Yeah.”

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.720
“Did you hear me?”

00:04:21.814 --> 00:04:22.814
“Uh-uh”

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.080
Still, despite him dumping her on&nbsp;
the spot, Rory still pines for him.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.240
To make things more uncomfortable, Dean&nbsp;
mutters Rory's name the night before his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:37.360
rushed wedding to another woman. Even worse?&nbsp;
Rory and Dean hook up during the marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.480
which ends with his belongings scattered on the&nbsp;
lawn. The divorce leads to one last attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.360
rekindle their toxic relationship, which to&nbsp;
be fair, should have been over years earlier.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.800
Most toxic relationships don't end with&nbsp;
the death of someone's entire family—but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.480
then, most people aren't Teen Wolf's Derek&nbsp;
Hale. His worst girlfriend, Kate Argent, enters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.200
the picture after Derek's first love, Paige,&nbsp;
dies from the werewolf bite he orchestrated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.320
Derek is riddled with guilt, which makes&nbsp;
seducing him all too easy for Kate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.240
The 20-something werewolf hunter inserts&nbsp;
herself into teenage Derek's life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.480
convincing him she loves him. Why? So she&nbsp;
can burn his entire family alive, obviously.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.720
When Derek is magically turned&nbsp;
back into his 15-year-old self,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.920
Kate ditches her murder plans and decides to use&nbsp;
him to gain access to his family's vault instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:31.600
Kate and Derek certainly weren't&nbsp;
destined for wedding bells,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.000
and hopefully the former hunter is ringing&nbsp;
Hell's bells somewhere fiery in the afterlife.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.640
Harley Quinn needs to stop calling&nbsp;
the Joker Puddin' and throw a pudding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:45.920
pie in his face instead. In her very first&nbsp;
appearance in Batman: the Animated Series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.960
Mistah J roughly shoves Harley to the other side&nbsp;
of his desk without a second thought — and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:56.000
abuse towards her only gets worse from there.&nbsp;
The Joker moves from shoving her onto his desk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.320
to throwing her out the window . And, he&nbsp;
continually chips away at her confidence.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.800
It's baffling that people still&nbsp;
call the couple "relationship goals"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.920
because they're anything but. Luckily, there's&nbsp;
always Birds of Prey, which follows a version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.320
of Harley who's finally cut the Joker out&nbsp;
of her life, and the Harley Quinn series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:18.240
which sees her enter into a far more&nbsp;
healthy relationship with Poison Ivy.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.520
How do you doom a marriage before it&nbsp;
even begins? Say your ex's name during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.040
the wedding ceremony — it works&nbsp;
out great for Ross on Friends.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.960
“I Ross”

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.920
“Take thee, Emily”

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:31.600
“Take thee, Rachel”

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.280
Though they're often considered the TV&nbsp;
darlings of the '90s, Ross and Rachel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:41.920
bring out the nastiest sides of each other in&nbsp;
their decade of will-they-or-won't-they drama.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.120
Ross' long-time obsession with Rachel leads&nbsp;
to his insecurity in their relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.560
causing him to question almost everything Rachel&nbsp;
does when they're dating or even broken up. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.840
he doesn't deem himself worthy of her, he begins&nbsp;
to act unworthy of her. Funny how that works!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.560
Rachel isn't without blame either:&nbsp;
Their couple is fraught with jealousy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.760
and manipulation on both ends. And to Ross'&nbsp;
dismay, "being on a break" does not warrant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:13.120
hooking up with someone just hours after pausing&nbsp;
the relationship with your so-called dream girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.600
Ross and Rachel are one of the most&nbsp;
unsatisfying endgame pairs on TV.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:23.520
What happens when you take a wannabe playboy and&nbsp;
pair him with a clingy romantic on and off for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:30.080
seven years? Nothing good. Whereas most toxic&nbsp;
TV relationships have at least some redeeming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.000
aspects, The Office's Ryan and&nbsp;
Kelly are a hot mess from the jump.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.760
Ryan only wants Kelly when she&nbsp;
starts dating someone else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.640
yet he completely disregards the fact that Kelly&nbsp;
wants a real, romantic relationship that ends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:49.120
in wedding bells. Meanwhile, Kelly uses unknowing&nbsp;
men to make Ryan jealous. A vicious cycle ensues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.760
in which Ryan sabotages those relationships,&nbsp;
only to bail on her right after they hook up.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:59.600
They're both also incredibly manipulative, whether&nbsp;
we're talking about Kelly faking a pregnancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:04.800
or Ryan proposing to her when she finally moves&nbsp;
on, fully admitting he'll probably change his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:10.640
mind later. Finally, we see some character&nbsp;
development when Kelly turns down Ryan's proposal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.440
She gets happily married to a sweet and loving&nbsp;
doctor and leaves Scranton to start her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:21.280
with him. But because Kelly and Ryan can't seem to&nbsp;
live apart, Ryan ditches his infant son and runs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:26.640
away with Kelly in the series finale. Goodbye,&nbsp;
character development. Hello, life of misery.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:32.480
Gossip Girl’s Chuck and Blair take the cake&nbsp;
for torment and betrayal: The couple just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:37.280
can't quit each other, or their vicious games. To&nbsp;
Chuck and Blair's credit, though, at least they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.280
acknowledge that they're toxic together. They&nbsp;
just don't care enough to throw in the towel.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.000
Their pattern of dangerous mind games&nbsp;
persists right to the very end of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.000
when they have a quickie wedding so Blair&nbsp;
doesn't have to testify against Chuck.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.160
There's nothing more romantic than a rushed&nbsp;
wedding ceremony with sirens blaring in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:59.920
background, shortly after killing your own&nbsp;
father. Manhattan's elite needs a lot of therapy.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.160
All the best romances begin&nbsp;
with someone turning their ex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:08.240
in to the cops, right? Orange Is&nbsp;
the New Black's Alex and Piper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:12.480
are so afraid of being without each other&nbsp;
that they throw each other into incarceration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.760
just so they don't have to be alone. Underneath&nbsp;
the possessive behavior, jealousy, and frequent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:22.240
cheating, the couple does love each other —&nbsp;
but boy, do they make each other prove it.

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:28.480
So, how can a relationship survive after both&nbsp;
partners have narc-ed on each other repeatedly? By&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:34.160
being physically intimate, obviously! When Piper&nbsp;
is released from prison and Alex is still inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.320
Alex tries to set Piper free when she's&nbsp;
transferred to a prison further away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.480
But apparently, this doesn't take.&nbsp;
The series' final moments see Piper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:47.200
visiting Alex in her new digs, determined&nbsp;
to make their prison marriage work. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.680
the ending would be a lot more satisfactory&nbsp;
if fans hadn't spent seven years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.120
watching the couple make each other&nbsp;
absolutely miserable in prison.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.400
At first, it's easy to sympathize with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.520
Lex Luthor's bad luck in the&nbsp;
love department on Smallville.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:07.840
His first wife uses him for his riches, after all.&nbsp;
But nothing excuses what he does to Lana Lang.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:13.360
Lex's laundry list of shady activity&nbsp;
includes putting cameras in Lana's bedroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.280
when she moves into the Luthor mansion,&nbsp;
cutting her off from friends and family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:20.320
and making sure she doesn't find&nbsp;
out that Clark still loves her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:25.680
If that weren't bad enough, Lex drugs her&nbsp;
into thinking she's pregnant. Given that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:30.000
he becomes a mad scientist, it's not a complete&nbsp;
stretch that he would pull something like this.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.080
After playing doctor with her hormone levels,&nbsp;
Lex tricks Lana into marrying him, using the fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:42.000
pregnancy to squash her hesitation. As his first&nbsp;
wife tricked Lex into marriage with pheromones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.320
you'd think Lex would be a little less&nbsp;
gung-ho about doing the same thing to someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:52.880
he supposedly cares about. Apparently not. It's&nbsp;
hard to watch Lex go from the caring, empathetic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:59.824
guy we see in season one to this monster.&nbsp;
Really, Lex should probably just stop dating.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.880
They say you should marry your best friend, but&nbsp;
no one says you should marry your frenemy. Yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:10.240
Al and Peg Bundy act like they hate each other&nbsp;
in almost every Married with Children episode.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:14.960
Their toxic dynamic is played for laughs that&nbsp;
probably seemed funnier in the '80s than they do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:21.760
now. Between Peg's savage barbs about Al's hygiene&nbsp;
and Al's continued mockery of Peg's unemployment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.840
one wonders: Do they even like each other?

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:29.280
Sure, they're possessive of each other, but&nbsp;
that comes across more like ownership than love.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:34.560
When Peg suspects Al of cheating on her,&nbsp;
she disguises herself as an exotic dancer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:39.200
at the club he frequents, making him fall&nbsp;
in love with her in that disguise. The guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.600
can't even recognize his own wife at a&nbsp;
dance club. But even worse than that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:48.960
He's cheating on his wife with ... his&nbsp;
wife. This marriage is a mess and a half.

